.011393041,-0.068221115,-0.03645428,0.041184988,-0.00074738206,-0.041712366,-0.04491226,0.035699844,-0.023760766,-0.009363482,-0.006066925,-0.064027175,-0.066053994,0.009994353,0.04535763,-0.05576658,-0.0011656433,0.07363131,-0.024604445,0.07323725,-0.004416629,-0.031933468,-0.021046666,0.01248461,-0.04850937,0.02705572,0.07219513,-0.03381654,-0.030952897,-0.035012413,-0.024125993,-0.020978555,-0.01691855,-0.02219055,-0.057248037,0.0060666082,-0.02079432,-0.027363267,-0.013001471,-0.011429188,-0.015098671,-0.020774703,0.050553113,-0.030073954,0.035177648,0.011901809,0.024567835,-0.0018424005,-0.019352684,0.0075336546,0.0012896797,-0.0263038,-0.06719125,-0.05370013,0.044079207,-0.025788527,0.01297526,0.018032977,0.033206552,-0.019108409,-0.05902751,-0.032482103,0.005917072,-0.009788668,0.0004000957,-0.0694901,-0.016207725,0.011451029,0.004187716,0.00156832,-0.0046518315,0.023745503,-0.00003482644,0.017508399,-0.01520845,-0.03453859,0.049103588,-0.012343347,0.010482878,0.006170837,-0.013989392,-0.045655105,0.003347446,-0.04534502,0.04049778,0.015656175,0.012343672,0.037299223,-0.004976752,-0.06588394,-0.0016812191,0.019553397,-0.020099146,0.041015647,-0.032459397,-0.05323239,0.0042689056,0.013535038,0.014334743,-0.02982904,0.017679408,0.15194641,0.016546315,0.0058301077,-0.025941353,0.024976643,0.024094127,0.015545317,-0.05753991,-0.020216346,0.027548883],"hash":"ee9bba8c:1829","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-16T14:25:06.315Z\n- **User:** /openspec:apply\n- **Outcome:** Apliquei a mudança. **A causa raiz era uma coisa mínima**: o `C4`. ## O que eu descobri Reimplementei o SimpleModulus em Python e testei offline com a chave de recepção do log — o **C3 do login decodifica perfeitamente**: ``` RECV #15 C3 len=233 chave=recv plaintext=00 F3 03 25 34 07 ... ← o F3 03 (character info) RECV #16 C4 len=784 ← O INVENTÁRIO ESTÁ AQUI ``` E no log do byp (build anterior) já aparecia `C3-SM decodificado len=167 : 00 F3 03 25 34 07 ...` — **a decifra S→C funcionava**. O que faltava era: > **`F3 10` (lista de itens) vem num C4 de 784 bytes** (≈60 itens × 13 bytes), e o `C4` tem header de **3 bytes** (C4, sizeHi, sizeLo) — o `TryDecodeSmBody` só tratava `C3` (2 bytes). Por isso o inventário nunca chegava, e sem ele o byp não tinha como saber qual slot tem potion. ## O que implementei (Fases 1–4) | Fase | Entrega | |---|---| | 1 | `TryDecodeSmBody` trata **C4** (header 3 bytes); buffer de decifra 512 → **2048** (o C4 de 784 decifra 568) | | 2 | `F3 10` → `slot → item ID` (o `DecodeItemId` do byp já batia com o `ItemByteConvert` do servidor — conferi) | | 3 | **Slots de HP/MP descobertos pelo ID** (`7168..7171` = HP, `7172..7174` = MP, elite `7238/7239`) → escolha automática, **sem beber potion nunca** | | 4 | **`VerifyAutoUse()`**: se o uso não produziu efeito em 900ms → o slot está vazio → **troca para o próximo do mesmo tipo** (round-robin) e registra no log; sem mais slots → avisa e **para de injetar** (hoje ele martela o slot morto e o log mente) | O le…\n- **Tools:** search_files, read_file, edit_file, manage_todos","vector":[0.017585125,0.030263087,-0.14217892,-0.07105349,0.055446383,-0.05889011,0.050470013,0.018089205,-0.051219285,-0.059417456,-0.06669727,0.014624272,0.061062947,-0.018684078,0.024027651,0.0058840583,-0.016775344,-0.064502284,-0.02754593,0.06069472,0.029344125,-0.047376245,-0.040272918,-0.004262184,0.08070829,0.028621003,0.015151483,0.041199397,-0.04482682,-0.017974582,0.01719035,0.0025422287,0.015722284,-0.032963675,0.0037186483,-0.05728527,0.058365833,-0.009136146,0.018000854,0.02956475,-0.009361756,-0.01575745,0.021463508,0.0287705,0.044764183,0.013117575,0.048881173,0.0015537251,0.047306087,-0.11047344,0.04109816,0.011926574,0.01528136,-0.039509088,0.07296462,0.037128985,-0.03329097,0.019861557,0.04672336,-0.017653,0.108680844,0.013133164,-0.013247898,0.070543475,0.022448119,-0.0112792775,-0.024237694,0.04216034,-0.