` do byp lia o **grupo do item** nos **bits 3..6** do byte 5. O servidor grava nos **bits 4..7**: ```cpp // MuEmu-master/eMU/GameServer/GameServer/ItemManager.cpp:1638 lpMsg[5] |= (item.m_Index & GET_ITEM(15,0)) >> 5; // grupo → bits 4..7 do byte5 ``` O grupo saía **pela metade**. Proof: o `F3 10` decodificado está no log (`gg_bypass2_s2c.log`), e a tabela de nomes do cliente (`Data\\Local\\Eng\\ItemTooltip_eng.txt`, texto puro: `grupo<TAB>indice<TAB>\"Nome\"`) permite conferir: | item | decode **antigo** | decode **novo** | |---|---|---| | slot 16 | `0x1C07` → \"Siege Potion\" (falso positivo) | (15,7) → **Scroll of Twister** | | slot 17 | `0x1C0B` → \"Box of Luck\" | (15,11) → **Scroll of Aqua Beam** | | slot 1 | `0x180B` → \"Summoning Orb\" | (6,11) → **Serpent Shield** | | slot 3 | `0x0019` → \"Sword Dancer\" | (8,25) → **Light Plate Armor** | 21 de 21 itens coerentes com o decode novo. O antigo produzia lixo (e falso \"Siege Potion\", que nem é HP). ## O que mudou **byp** - `AutoPotion.cpp:933` — `DecodeItemId` corrigido (grupo = nibble alto do byte 5). - `AutoPotion.cpp:90` — tabela `POTIONS[]` com **ID + nome**: 14,0..6, 14,38..40, 14,70/71 e **13,117..120 \"Vitality Potion\"** (exclusivo deste server). `IsHpPotionId`/`IsMpPotionId` agora consultam a tabela (não mais faixa de IDs). - `AutoPotion.cpp:1107/1133` — **`F3 14`** (item modificado) e **`C1 28`** (item removido): a tabela `slot → ID` passa a s…\n- **Tools:** search_files, glob, skill, read_file, manage_todos, edit_file, git","vector":[0.035438765,0.061154105,-0.14965796,-0.010384861,0.06917394,-0.05870097,0.017630057,0.012319048,-0.044667196,0.0005999735,-0.023703974,0.04594688,0.072499305,-0.008960135,0.029585272,0.004923182,-0.011539901,-0.025678715,-0.053896606,0.05806321,0.029170636,-0.022819785,-0.053316172,-0.026592718,0.06410738,0.0456173,-0.0131606,0.05098614,-0.020450344,-0.0006007045,0.023208208,0.00085984654,0.009539872,-0.024473058,-0.01115306,-0.057610203,0.06638207,-0.031667326,-0.00010