` openspec list multi-instance-muproxy 0/18 tasks hwid-viewer 0/14 tasks dark-ui-muproxy 0/21 tasks ``` | change | arquivos | o que resolve | |---|---|---| | `multi-instance-muproxy` | proposal + design + tasks + 2 specs (`muproxy-multi-instance`, `player-hud`) | N MuProxy2 convivendo, cada um com seu `main.exe`; portas por instância; **adotar** jogo já rodando; título `MuProxy \\| HexDL \\| 214 \\| Lorencia \\| 120, 150` | | `hwid-viewer` | proposal + design + tasks + spec (`hwid-management`) | **ver** o HWID que o cliente manda no login e **substituir** por um valor escolhido (ou aleatório) | | `dark-ui-muproxy` | proposal + design + tasks + spec (`muproxy-ui`) | tema escuro, inputs organizados (label acima, em grade, cards), LEDs de estado, header do char | ## As 3 decisões que eu tomei (fácil reverter) 1. **HWID = texto livre validado + botão \"gerar\"** — cobre tanto \"restaurar o HWID antigo depois de reinstalar o SO\" quanto \"quero dois HWIDs diferentes\". Validação estrita do formato `8HEX-8HEX-8HEX-8HEX`. 2. **Multi-instância = adota também jogo já rodando** — o byp já tem loop de retry; fazer ele **re-resolver a porta a cada falha** custa quase nada e dá a feature de graça. 3. **UX = restyle WinForms agora** (sem NuGet, sem reescrita); WebView2 fica pra um change separado, se ainda faltar. ## Detalhes…\n- **Tools:** read_file, search_files, write_file, edit_file, repl, run_command, manage_todos","vector":[-0.010512442,0.036721896,-0.17354141,-0.013385287,0.05927607,-0.049799465,0.030273145,-0.01568431,-0.003916687,-0.009295817,0.004395293,-0.016352328,0.09204779,-0.017636554,-0.0116061075,0.009922973,0.023469986,-0.05481871,-0.04216764,0.03209167,0.021951614,-0.065847516,-0.06548974,0.010249674,0.08912449,0.055935953,0.001278156,0.048283864,-0.04806605,-0.00883572,0.036435295,0.021830639,0.027161168,-0.024860943,0.01321551,-0.04926391,0.09333004,-0.010931883,0.016683174,0.0022220702,-0.0012153065,-0.019627422,0.016144425,-0.0063483436,0.026255095,-0.01128