,0.028118422,0.04712379,-0.026638683,-0.042198617,-0.0067179217,-0.0129195945,-0.022583116,-0.00045992047,-0.024790376,-0.05691582,-0.029318139,0.00018038957,-0.043219693,0.020889012,-0.0026712723,-0.02348009,-0.029052168,0.038638696,-0.023887962,0.0011300744,0.01091975,0.03771637,-0.016817795,0.05772776,0.009919185,-0.02914617,0.00597661,-0.035324775,-0.021943754,0.02576793,-0.031377472,-0.024990935,0.0046863263,0.025332337,-0.005589695,-0.07363017,-0.022311281,0.008785461,0.039306205,-0.01851397,-0.09064364,0.04008659,0.02673676,-0.011627757,0.0353352,0.008598509,-0.007233539,0.0012468714,-0.022553172,-0.06354132,-0.038021434,0.009494497,0.00048899505,-0.021901168,-0.013833498,0.016510418,-0.052251086,-0.012145464,-0.06899916,-0.017470712,-0.027776673,0.027785877,-0.024337925,0.006653356,-0.0426046,0.031203574,-0.0018833345,-0.02302817,0.050116647,-0.02209196,-0.046411507,-0.02039842,0.002816423,0.011676132,0.0068045147,0.004490059,0.12917066,-0.0017095448,0.017328637,-0.021523984,0.04851227,0.051748537,-0.031013003,-0.05441985,-0.017842337,0.024876822],"hash":"239ea08c:2038","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-16T19:15:47.957Z\n- **User:** ultimo erro apos sua change [2026-11-16 10:46:39] [PACKETSNIFFER] recv() ret=12 socket=1640 [2026-11-16 10:46:39] [PACKETSNIFFER] S->C #7: hdr=2 op=F1 len=12 [C1 0C F1 00 01 33 08 33 31 2E 00 00 ] [2026-11-16 10:46:39] [PACKETSNIFFER] recv() ret=27 socket=816 [2026-11-16 10:46:39] [PACKETHANDLER] RECV linha (25): [ATTACK_PLAYERIDX|idx=3308] [2026-11-16 10:46:39] [GAMEMEMORY] LocalPlayerIndex setado para 0x3308 [2026-11-16 10:46:39] [ATTACK] PLAYERIDX setado: 0x3308 [2026-11-16 10:46:39] [GAMEMEM…\n- **Outcome:** **Causa raiz do crash encontrada e corrigida.** ## O que era O crash não era do jogo — era do **nosso hook do gerador de HWID**. Correlação no log: *todo* AV em `USER32+0x292A0` apareceu depois da linha `[HWID] hook do gerador instalado` (10:11:17, 10:27:36, 10:35:55, 10:39:31, 10:46:40). O AV de 06:42 era outro (em `main.exe`). Reverse do binário (SysWOW64/USER32.dll, `wsprintfA` em RVA `0x29260`): ``` wsprintfA: lea eax,[ebp+10h]; push eax; push [ebp+0Ch]; push [ebp+8]; call wvsprintfA; pop ebp; ret → CDECL (ret puro, quem limpa é o caller: add esp,0x18 no cliente) wvsprintfA: ... mov ebx,[ebp+0Ch] ; mov cl,[ebx] ← 0x292A0, o ponto do AV ``` O `mov cl,[ebx]` lê o **ponteiro de formato**: `EBX=0x14` / `0x1000` = lixo. Ou seja, o hook passava `fmt` inválido. Motivo: `HookWsprintfA` lia os argumentos com `__asm { mov eax,[esp+4] ... }` — mas o prólogo do MSVC (`sub esp,28h` + 4 pushes) já deslocou o ESP, então os slots lidos eram lixo. O `buf`/`fmt` saíam errados. ## Correção (`byp/gg_bypass2/src/hwid/HwidManager.cpp:74`) - Hook agora tem a **mesma assinatura do original** (`int __cdecl HookWsprintfA(char*, const char*, unsigned×4)`) — o compilador cuida dos slots, sem leitura crua de pilha. - Guarda de sanidade: só age se `fmt` começa com `\"%08X\"` (se o RVA do patch estiver errado, não mexe em nada). - O override passa a ser escrito direto no buffer que o cliente acabou de formatar (`strncpy_s(buf, 36, ...)`), sem depender do slot. - Comentários/correções de RVA: o call-site …\n- **Tools:** list_directory, search_files, read_file, glob, write_file, edit_file, repl, run_command, memory, manage_todos","vector":[0.032114916,0.036716413,-0.14850618,-0.037939124,0.07287131,-0.05271328,0.037856765,0.00077453844,-0.039290108,-0.013623518,-0.020842284,0.030094892,0.06648903,-0.023500519,0.040316317,-0.010235576,-0.024599817,0.0015160724,-0.06744441,-0.010648428,-0.0006003879,-0.053961527,-0.036817618,0.03304282,0.10637899,0.015207277,0.0008725578,0.047930192,-0.0357323,-0.008804332,0.05507189,-0.00914238,0.0025279708,-0.07090992,0.0071093277,-0.042479984,-0.001718586,-0.048019536,0.0030165592,0.03206795,-0.008887233,-0.019716911,0.04910736,0.004428009,-0.015619706,-0.01691277,0.07954217,0