81,-0.009643028,-0.046312924,-0.01776292,-0.008539379,0.041471053,-0.031788882,0.03623199,0.04011912,0.033866227,0.1220836,-0.010990731,-0.017205024,0.025673676,0.03620796,-0.023772726,-0.004553369,0.0064101145,-0.03470524,-0.018367045,-0.0050971624,-0.027246205,-0.014962209,-0.010388671,-0.06572778,0.008999813,-0.021807797,-0.05841964,-0.025094697,-0.0088523,0.011379268,-0.025668424,-0.0375476,-0.010790306,-0.05020809,0.026974622,-0.011114922,0.037495423,0.0078007584,0.005160654,-0.03574296,-0.033982493,-0.039596535,-0.03021252,-0.028679125,-0.019224469,-0.02645643,0.027588386,0.008268759,0.020322427,0.04151396,-0.058415968,0.010136766,0.0011569434,0.053033438,0.0095296325,-0.05490582,-0.011962921,0.02818123,0.0078424765,0.007993049,-0.017320901,0.0029368675,0.02763532,0.042644363,-0.031550508,0.014422037,0.026067104,0.0027895526,-0.0033557124,-0.043093517,0.007752225,-0.03518014,-0.03857346,-0.039962564,0.030814866,-0.019568505,0.017051227,-0.02320765,0.0045062453,0.009471433,0.028198242,-0.0010011204,-0.019661278,0.044483054,-0.021203287,-0.029333666,0.039547827,-0.052071154,0.012391174,-0.025378348,0.0069923284,0.13523218,0.03532347,-0.008080869,-0.03145814,0.018159982,0.026239445,0.0026184998,-0.022030676,0.037719894,0.028139157],"hash":"139bde41:1638","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-16T20:10:57.848Z\n- **User:** acabei de testar novamente, e ainda assim deu pau com user diferente...\n- **Outcome:** Achei **dois bugs meus** no log da tua última sessão (`sessions\\base100\\gg_bypass2.log`): ## Bug 1 — o patch do `FindWindowA` nunca entrou ``` [12:06:31] [CLIENT] call [FindWindowA] nao encontrado no Main.dll — patch cancelado ``` Eu procurava `FF 15 <endereço da função>` (o **valor** dentro do slot da IAT) em vez de `FF 15 <endereço do slot da IAT>` (o que o `call [IAT]` referencia de fato). Por isso o patch era cancelado → a checagem de instância única continuava matando a 2ª instância. Corrigi e **validei offline**: simulei a relocação do loader (base `0x682F0000`) e o padrão `FF 15 74 84 4F 68` aparece **1 e só 1 lugar**, em `RVA 0x13E6B0` ✔. O scan agora só olha seções executáveis (nada de patch em `.data`). ## Bug 2 — o override manual anulava o HWID por instância ``` [HWID] override definido: 12BA1074-EC4F9BAF-00000000-15CB2022 ``` Esse valor vem do botão **\"Usar o do cliente\"** (o HWID da máquina) e estava salvo em `muproxy_hwid_100.txt`. Ele era aplicado *verbatim* → as duas instâncias iam com o **mesmo** HWID → o servidor derrubava a 2ª conta. Agora a variação por instância (último grupo = `hash(base)`) vale **também sobre o override**: o override define a \"parte da máquina\", e a instância garante o final diferente. Na base 0 (1ª instância) o valor vai verbatim, como sempre. ## O que a tua sessão mostrava (antes dos fixes) - **base100 (2ª)**: conectou no login server ✔, pegou o server list ✔, conectou no GS (porta 46001, base 100 ✔) e **morreu 3s depois** — sem gera…\n- **Tools:** edit_file, run_command, repl, manage_todos","vector":[0.05903905,0.030929608,-0.15910593,-0.02359657,0.051275566,-0.02834207,0.02803163,0.028876368,-0.02968462,-0.023096174,-0.009635078,0.021470295,0.052037064,-0.01504966,0.047761127,-0.017835658,-0.019914804,-0.04473861,-0.051226113,-0.009280425,0.028050296,-0.013669276,-0.053472426,-0.005430349,0.07611058,0.02622679,0.014936976,0.07538719,-0.027110573,-0.0017942404,0.029195156,0.0308,0.02084255,-0.052272964,-0.014622136,-0.039784852,0.03188813,-0.025109332,-0.01841887,0.031736393,0.01438491,-0.062159758,0.012085864,-0.0003556856,0.0064063715,0.023635428,0.056183603,0.0649328,0.07993019,-0.06760356,0.035699837,0.0019161287,0.018380282,-0.06265768,0.09612557,0.002781331,-0.048244648,0.012661219,0.013964541,-0.05059666,0.077476695,0.0075323884,-0.013447618,0.095622145,-0.046150554,-0.025948435,-0.059100002,0.0039964323,-0.0046267845,-0.007642573,0.05773234,0.020495089,0.017748108,0.0