,-0.038042367,-0.059609108,-0.10255298,-0.021372002,0.06666243,-0.035249975,0.026052892,0.045210477,-0.0024049408,0.07326024,-0.0078077405,-0.04489653,-0.011855498,0.012929291,0.005403244,0.009808556,0.039252374,-0.001884185,-0.058302347,0.005692413,-0.01709536,-0.008007048,-0.013779235,-0.03382769,-0.036790255,-0.011678469,-0.045233212,-0.041755006,0.034229323,0.019136166,-0.015422859,0.023315888,0.051768847,0.0053372583,0.010332316,-0.014125107,0.047200438,-0.05260451,0.008241877,-0.036124673,0.01066127,-0.03341787,0.004126869,-0.013222419,0.018720731,-0.07761406,0.040124044,-0.004891123,0.027984807,-0.021993944,-0.031683657,0.0036689725,0.0024549286,0.029284202,-0.01664172,-0.05309153,-0.016071355,-0.012149805,0.001749979,0.0067700977,-0.05732937,0.010100857,-0.009466923,-0.0060349074,-0.016280552,-0.0003657804,0.05717463,0.013113801,0.005776623,-0.02853906,-0.037161108,-0.028300999,-0.025810923,-0.048772484,0.012230837,-0.021258827,0.039958414,0.026600368,0.01905349,-0.03423472,-0.027260864,-0.009796411,-0.03701008,0.04012867,-0.019589072,-0.05828283,0.054424748,0.0052059367,0.0018781754,0.009661579,0.04672274,0.0825833,0.015868671,0.0067008575,-0.070371985,0.03196031,0.041043907,0.026814627,-0.04722495,-0.030449094,0.008558347],"hash":"2ee6e1b5:1826","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-16T20:52:11.963Z\n- **User:** acho que deve ser ip de rede isso nao? pq eu to no msm ip, deveria bloquear assim, o pc principal ta com uma instancia, nesse msm pc tem uma vm e vc ta dentro da vm junto com outro que roda normal... entao nao e ip e algo no cliente acho... se for algo no server pode ser ip de rede?\n- **Outcome:** Sim — **é o server, e é o IP.** Mas tem um detalhe que muda tudo: o servidor **não vê o IP de rede**, ele vê o **IP público**, e ele **conta as sessões de todas as máquinas que saem atrás do mesmo NAT**. ## A topologia real (medi agora na VM) ``` PC principal (NAT 192.168.71.2) ── WAN ──► 186.235.202.26 ├── instância do host = sessão 1 desse IP └── VM (192.168.71.128) ──┬── base0 (funciona) = sessão 2 desse IP └── base100 (dc) = sessão 3 ← REJEITADA ``` IP público da VM: **186.235.202.26** (confirmado via ipify) — o **mesmo** do PC principal, porque o host faz NAT da VM. No código do eMU (`eMU/GameServer/GameServer/`): - `SocketManager.cpp:719` → `gIpManager.CheckIpAddress(inet_ntoa(SocketAddr.sin_addr))` → **`inet_ntoa` do socket aceito = IP pós-NAT = 186.235.202.26**. O servidor nunca vê o `192.168.71.128`. - `IpManager.cpp:34` → rejeita quando `IpAddressCount >= m_MaxIpConnection`. - `ServerInfo.cpp:2761` → valor vem de **`GameServer.ini` → `[GameServerInfo] MaxIpConnection`**. Ou seja: **o contador é por IP público, e é compartilhado entre o host e a VM**. Teu \"outro PC sai pelo mesmo IP e roda normal\" não contradiz nada — ele simplesmente está **dentro** do limite; a base100 é a que **estoura**. Pelo teu relato, `MaxIpConnection` = **2** (host + base0 ocupam as 2 vagas; a base100 é a 3ª). ## Previsão testável (1 minuto) **Fecha a instância do PC principal** (não só a base0) e relança a base100 → ela deve **entrar** (vira a 2ª sessão de 186.235.202.26). Se ainda assim fal…\n- **Tools:** run_command","vector":[0.007627795,0.08677328,-0.14230856,-0.017021524,0.017923065,-0.04204624,0.015356068,0.00079844403,-0.046267547,-0.043242667,-0.029736128,0.019506631,-0.009879009,-0.053201314,-0.0059059253,-0.03527809,-0.047796067,-0.045701187,-0.07867121,0.019986458,-0.032409444,-0.08841776,-0.036672097,-0.030411288,0.060429752,0.037120163,0.004850641,0.02795933,-0.0042263465,-0.030673567,0.011893707,-0.0035384549,0.011731982,-0.014299594,-0.0062608505,-0.011082124,-0.0013438074,0.00042108903,-0.033988904,-0.0015961978,0.024597773,-0.120467804,-0.02794872,-0.014862596,-0.026700446,0.003820739,0.0068987263,0.0026130243,0.04554233,-0.08572016,0.052637007,-0.010604098,-0.020072334,-0.059046123,0.07422315,0.0028767714,-0.005352