0.008507983,-0.012270231,0.019910466,-0.011070898,0.023172757,-0.03172208,-0.027245281,-0.0012277963,-0.000836844,-0.018788308,0.044767115,-0.039642505,0.029575165,0.0041524596,-0.021129996,-0.015202857,-0.029561626,0.06090448,-0.01188994,-0.012688693,-0.04649172,-0.018950976,-0.00927453,-0.008634113,-0.0026694278,0.03602033,-0.0012539547,0.03769321,0.022423344,-0.0035978172,-0.050281607,0.013089258,0.013590617,-0.0064125843,0.07600079,-0.007836979,-0.0376015,0.008981267,-0.0013912666,0.01855248,0.0014233789,0.035235938,0.09944653,0.031400234,0.031676102,-0.018097809,0.04621426,0.043282706,-0.0064584245,-0.058953166,-0.03505518,-0.021139596],"hash":"2fa032a6:254","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-16T21:00:54.987Z\n- **User:** mas eu to com mais de um main no msm ip publico e nao deu pau... o problema e mais de 1 no msm computador\n- **Outcome:** ## Fechado: **é o servidor, e é o contador por IP** — agora com prova lado a lado O MuProxy2 grava log em arquivo (`logs\\muproxy2_<hora>.log`). Comparei as duas rodadas: | | base 0 (entrou no jogo) | base 100 (dc) | |---|---|---| | `[C116] Porta do GS detectada` | 12:11:24.690 | 12:12:02.106 | | `[PROXY] Ouvindo 127.0.0.1:…` | 45901 | 46001 | | `[PROXY] Conectado ao servidor real …:45901` | 12:11:24.934 | 12:12:02.348 | | resposta do GS | **greeting de 12 bytes** | **silêncio** | **O proxy se comportou EXATAMENTE igual nos dois casos.** Logo a recusa é do servidor — e a única variável do lado do servidor que difere é **a ordem da conexão**: a base 0 foi a conexão *n* daquele IP **com a sessão anterior ainda viva**; a base 100 foi a seguinte. ### Por que \"2 mains no mesmo IP público funciona\" — medi a topologia ``` PC principal (NAT 192.168.71.2) ──► IP público 186.235.202.26 ├── instância do PC principal = sessão 1 desse IP └── VM (192.168.71.128) ──┬── base0 = sessão 2 desse IP └── base100 = sessão 3 ← RECUSADA ``` O contador (`IpManager.cpp:34`) é **por IP público** e **soma todas as máquinas atrás do mesmo NAT**. Os 2 mains que tu viu funcionando estavam **dentro** do limite; a base100 é a que **estoura**. O \"ip de rede\" (192.168.71.128) o servidor nunca vê — ele conta o público. ### Teste decisivo (1 minuto) **Fecha a instância do PC PRINCIPAL** (não só a base0) e relança a base100 → ela deve **entrar** (vira a 2ª sessão do IP). Se ainda falhar, é `MaxIpConnection = 1`. E…\n- **Tools:** search_files, mcp_tool, edit_file, glob, ask_user, desktop_snapshot, read_file, run_command, manage_todos","vector":[0.017636405,0.09453319,-0.15104961,-0.008625044,0.01726896,-0.05935132,0.01652225,0.025596619,-0.046102744,-0.01301631,-0.01594274,0.005268581,0.020876158,-0.042924512,0.025639765,-0.022955395,0.014956719,-0.05587427,-0.070080295,0.024952099,-0.009716075,-0.05582619,-0.029888159,-0.025233159,0.067709126,0.049781032,0.025801696,0.030370023,0.020020476,-0.021591665,-0.009279356,0.029416548,0.009397717,-0.024293786,-0.03785808,-0.054317754,0.016716512,-0.029311486,-0.03973002,0.018346768,0.049044404,-0.11543064,0.0076567437,-0.006401098,0.0050683348,0.016457919,-0.010995554,0.016987076,0.05932025,-0.07275975,0.053528283,0.028008366,0.012902022,-0.047652572,0.08653885,0.003969084,-0.020895395,0.039074067,0.02930719,-0.054167274,0.10298173,0.013871556,0.008564896,0.0675391,-0.01896596,-0.023022292,-0.04950885,0.014867225,-0.015223193,0.011868267,-0.006674686,0.0031857758,0.05805075,0.014741759,0.035633378,-0.020976374,-0.009290652,-0.018991457,0.0037746804,0.00822608,0.049180392,0.008442892,0.11737752,-0.036777932,0.040850684,0.010842989,-0.06053184,0.0071749305,-0.048450958,0.09309478,-0.022293996,0.03363165,0.053524766,-0.023684641,-0.044728547,-0.00089617923,-0.05032939,0.005910635,-0.030997604,-0.01486158,-0.03699058,-0.009920431,0.04123237,-0.013678658,0.021154271,0.06627955,-0.0021023336,0.03783536,-0.001790458,-0.028544355,0.0030818114,0.04712794,-0.06678583,-0.027260305,0.0566