curam em 3 lugares (output dir, caminho legado, raiz) e **saem sem falhar** se não acharem, em vez de estourar. - `dotnet build MuProxy2.Tests` → **0 erros, 0 warnings** ✓ ## Aproveitei pra limpar a \"config no PC\" O override de HWID da base 100 estava salvo em `muproxy_hwid_100.txt` com o valor **`...BC5BDE2E-BFCE2333`** — que não é o HWID real do cliente (`BFCE2022`); é o valor já transformado, colado de volta no campo. Renomeei pra `.bak` → agora o byp usa o **HWID real do cliente** + a variação por instância. (Conferi no source do eMU: o `GameServer` **não** valida HWID de cliente — só a licença server↔AuthServer — e mesmo que validasse, isso viria *depois* do greeting, então não é a causa do DC.) ## Estado para o teste | | pronto | |---|---| | byp com hook de `getpeername` (peer real) | ✅ compilado + deployado em `F:\\blackrockmu`, `sessions\\base0`, `sessions\\base100` | | build do MuProxy2/Tests | ✅ 0 erros | | overrid…\n- **Tools:** search_files, desktop_list_windows, read_file, glob, edit_file, write_file, run_command, manage_todos","vector":[0.08006975,0.029259034,-0.16061226,0.008950857,0.041262537,-0.05253869,0.03298477,0.03781806,-0.031383675,-0.048380557,-0.035716284,0.042343773,0.051218085,-0.02314028,-0.02364054,0.010053038,0.008511919,-0.0055855946,-0.0477427,0.017815119,0.012399804,-0.047280546,-0.041033447,0.011191561,0.09126215,0.041537467,0.00019118156,0.028557252,-0.03458619,-0.05537722,0.08269114,-0.02288608,0.008039336,-0.06313228,-0.019728681,-0.05052534,0.0066872593,-0.018104529,0.01122503,0.028418478,0.02314594,-0.03678949,-0.021345751,-0.0017232847,0.030669533,0.027108677,0.059048794,0.039269168,0.08196169,-0.07698427,0.09435126,0.0032128443,0.059105232,-0.045133363,0.0748234,0.0009916682,-0.0057069026,0.049900122,0.02421331,-0.017501498,0.087674014,0.03287482,-0.017482182,0.08133667,0.0027604406,-0.038918767,-0.042361286,0.011251717,-0.021796975,-0.019281594,0.046716105,0.012324269,0.0038218296,-0.004513515,0.015687613,-0.019433418,-0.0