,-0.029245019,0.037460063,0.041345883,0.023590738,0.11120329,0.012885185,-0.031408377,0.000009528588,0.012676548,0.013085107,0.00603025,0.0440382,-0.02231788,-0.07001511,-0.022492003,0.007173599,-0.01687824,-0.0055651506,-0.022644972,-0.016444243,0.042196598,-0.054652166,-0.063877635,0.01856316,-0.009008211,0.0039023007,0.013854703,0.03321335,-0.029036624,0.008227128,-0.016371595,0.039661422,-0.015765397,-0.009223477,-0.0010780365,0.009977298,-0.02183359,-0.041198853,-0.020041827,0.03526937,-0.042465165,0.04912273,-0.01304033,0.01216487,-0.0020031612,-0.04171232,0.0024252404,0.046747845,-0.01931425,-0.015322832,-0.048449747,-0.022917274,-0.0118393395,-0.0015130646,0.008853809,-0.05799128,0.027167695,0.015504987,-0.007049082,-0.047151513,-0.031824794,0.017472263,0.021079328,-0.013354744,-0.023052506,-0.009208548,-0.040279128,-0.028221412,-0.02884511,0.044145156,-0.011879552,0.046795983,0.0018993901,0.023617027,-0.014486694,0.028068531,0.0043775486,-0.035580706,0.027642082,-0.03068027,-0.051291745,0.01924935,0.0030402078,-0.025503531,-0.0024995971,0.037360232,0.13274483,-0.005820662,-0.01524117,-0.055919286,0.015413953,0.008727426,-0.008712804,-0.055102788,-0.023309587,-0.0021116773],"hash":"9660c953:1895","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-16T22:07:12.270Z\n- **User:** 44411 nao pode mudar isso e p[orta de cs do servidor deles.... oq pode mudar sao nossas portas de comunicacao entrew muproxy e byp...\n- **Outcome:** Entendido — e você está certo: **as portas do servidor não podem ser encostadas**. Refiz o isolamento. ## O que mudou **Antes:** eu deslocava *tudo* por `+base` (44411→44511, GS 45901→46001). Funcionava, mas mexia na porta do servidor — violando a tua regra. **Agora:** a **porta fica intacta** (CS = 44411, GS = a do C116) e o que separa as instâncias é o **IP de loopback**: | | instância 0 | instância 1 | |---|---|---| | proxy do CS | `127.0.0.1:44411` | `127.0.0.2:44411` | | proxy do GS | `127.0.0.1:45901` | `127.0.0.2:45901` | | canal cmd (nosso) | `127.0.0.1:44412` | `127.0.0.1:44512` | | canal pkt (nosso) | `127.0.0.1:44413` | `127.0.0.1:44513` | O Windows escuta em todo o `127.0.0.0/8` — testei bind+connect em `127.0.0.2:44411` e `127.0.0.3:44411` aqui, funciona. ## Código - **byp**: o hook de connect agora **só troca o IP** (`InstancePorts::LocalIp()`), a porta fica igual (`WinsockHooks.cpp:376`). `InstancePorts::LocalPort()` — que deslocava a porta — foi removido. - **MuProxy2**: `InstanceAllocator.LocalIp` = `127.0.0.(base/100+1)`; `LoginPort` = 44400… **44411 fixo**; `GsPort(real)` = **a porta real, sem deslocar**. O `TcpLoopbackProxy` passou a escutar no `listenAddress` (o loopback da instância) em vez de 127.0.0.1 fixo, e o rewrite da server-list aponta para ele. - Teto de 9 instâncias (127.0.0.1…9), porque o rewrite do IP no payload tem que manter o tamanho do campo. ## Prova Teste novo `byp/MuProxy2/MuProxy2.Tests/InstanceIsolationTests.cs` — **2/2 passando**: ``…\n- **Tools:** edit_file, search_files, write_file, tool_search","vector":[0.029222641,0.041128587,-0.14673167,-0.024129998,0.027875725,-0.08040676,0.038050827,-0.005584629,-0.016330982,-0.020312758,-0.04474917,0.01752548,0.042547952,-0.04637083,0.045316074,-0.045240708,-0.039770797,-0.033752177,-0.04010704,0.017686637,-0.0033282894,-0.064027116,-0.021742297,-0.0104331095,0.08231684,0.04507447,0.01871867,0.024704063,-0.0098734675,-0.017440615,-0.0012784399,-0.0040357,0.004805053,-0.044674467,-0.04035211,-0.02750702,0.019420315,-0.031810645,-0.010469031,0.016024433,0.03136519,-0.07976825,0.0010590443,-0.02995079,0.03066344,-0.015476505,-0.010851093,0.016841257,0.06188129,-0.08510855,0.038207673,0.015117848,0.006446737,-0.02399965,0.05576153,0.03083143,-0.04610171,0.04880956,0.036093984,-0.02218456,0.06098857,0.0341365,0.007046798,0.10502107,-0.007391267,0.028602554,-0.04308572,0.01927474,-0.051611915,0.005009817,-0.0004854446,0.0010874727,0.03645