.039689608,-0.0077689313,-0.022332266,0.014754397,0.0014707163,0.019343534,0.011079045,-0.037778374,0.039402347,0.004435707,0.014358141,-0.0048911967,-0.03901106,0.07405402,0.028136296,-0.0020192808,-0.0016349395,-0.007996566,-0.042569082,-0.018015785,-0.0060096607,0.0033597837,-0.012579876,0.0726937,0.008696928,0.0008287469,-0.014529392,0.006898344,-0.023146257,-0.048019934,0.0622119,0.0023255348,-0.031960305,0.033234987,-0.0074042813,-0.018902622,0.020052087,0.031237165,0.10336444,0.0038694069,-0.0045263655,-0.06267652,0.046189245,0.024367243,-0.02188661,-0.039746266,-0.039772592,0.006937775],"hash":"f802ee4d:1752","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-16T22:10:48.324Z\n- **User:** duvida, estou so com um mu proxy aberto e abri o main.exe e apareceu server. isso deveria funcionar?\n- **Outcome:** **Sim, deveria funcionar — e funcionou.** Do nosso lado tudo passou. O que travou foi o **GS**. O log da sessão base100 (`sessions\\base100\\gg_bypass2.log`) mostra o caminho completo: ``` [14:09:26] [INSTANCE] identidade: pid=9380 base=100 (MUPROXY_BASE ok) [14:09:26] [TCPCLIENT] Conectado ao 127.0.0.1:44512 [14:09:26] [PACKETHANDLER] RECV linha (23): [HELLO_ACK|ok=1|base=100] ← handshake ok [14:09:26] [CLIENT] verificacao de entrada na sala neutralizada em 0x00414D0D ← patch do gate ok [14:09:32] SEND C1 6 bytes [C1 06 F4 03 00 00] ← pacote de sala ENVIADO [14:09:32] C116: porta do GS detectada = 45901 ← lista do CS chegou [14:09:32] CONNECT to 145.239.149.84:45901 → connect local 127.0.0.2:45901 ← GS DA INSTÂNCIA CERTA [14:10:01] S->C total=6 | opcodes: 00=1 F4=5 ← NENHUM greeting do GS ``` E o log do proxy (UI, instância base 100) dá o ponto exato: ``` [14:07:44.879] Conectado ao servidor real 145.239.149.84:45901 [14:07:45.113] Relay 45901:S->C: socket encerrado pelo servidor -> forcibly closed by the remote host ← RST do GS ~230 ms depois ``` Ou seja: o **GS aceitou o TCP e resetou 233 ms depois**, sem mandar o greeting (12 bytes F1). O cliente espera, cai e mostra o \"server\" na tela. É o mesmo sintoma de antes — **o GS só permite 1 sessão por IP público**. **Duas coisas que o log também revela:** 1. Na máquina há **duas** janelas do MuProxy2 (`base 0` PID 11816 e `base 100` PID 8024) e **dois** main.exe rodando — a janela do screenshot é a base 100 (`127.0.0.2`). A base …\n- **Tools:** edit_file, run_command","vector":[0.009343224,0.09256512,-0.1572479,-0.040281218,0.03193298,-0.06653952,0.029180933,0.0035841821,-0.01139485,-0.035389062,-0.042995516,0.035381287,0.060015082,-0.02549836,0.046315055,-0.040609322,-0.012844185,-0.06375617,-0.07493968,0.026035149,0.040347647,-0.065074004,-0.017659051,-0.034235235,0.07980941,0.04421866,0.022943309,0.056179617,-0.00829483,-0.044664867,0.017454086,0.03224034,0.0014370503,-0.015198683,-0.007796047,-0.03305719,-0.006344479,-0.03862216,-0.036539868,-0.0001437545,0.039011903,-0.07984345,0.0010202333,0.016291933,0.005575527,0.0007511897,0.042598356,0.045954976,0.0653145,-0.0638357,0.007109868,0.049772598,-0.004314411,-0.06364668,0.08724379,0.008127546,-0.03587798,0.03930471,0.013858763,-0.05366082,0.09680143,0.009481512,-0.011049383,0.07085393,0.00087532576,-0.030769559,-0.07891579,0.022972113,-0.0106406845,0.018965699,0.04165851,0.011484273,0.037029564,0.0013107363,0.014364837,0.0031143879,-0.041607745,-0.032545805,-0.00038143646,-0.00029737904,0.016280895,-0.008182951,0.11138046,-0.05140418,0.03412843,-0.012588663,-0.04609221,0.007268466,-0.060201112,0.09483928,0.022336306,-0.037476983,0.030083336,-0.017821956,-0.06734615,0.027860047,-0.045055587,0.015063198,-0.008244551,-0.006030182,-0.012748928,0.01205801,0.04172599,-0.014151667,0.016559662,0.07493555,-0.021214575,0.02535827,0.021901013,0.019220019,0.0051565804,0.047291964,-0.02994167,-0.06415948,0.047792133,-0.0054821423,0.047223683,-0.022257904,0.008617012,0.03030218,-0.059054397,-0.003940688,-0.016631683,0.02446898,0.043806378,-0.0055