03164995,0.03075154,0.023108093,-0.0027631281,-0.049536075,0.023383725,0.03610256,-0.0005830034,-0.005560661,0.016755208,0.0016414712,-0.058181483,0.018084047,-0.031065477,0.030222662,-0.037792128,0.039541446,0.010372126,-0.011064987,-0.020482993,0.03093143,0.009413858,-0.012270807,0.023670841,-0.023958262,-0.04056079,0.054931376,-0.019629428,0.0037284337,0.0052202265,0.010822861,0.14053221,0.016682945,-0.02065826,-0.07055424,0.048018448,0.029060135,-0.03291743,-0.045483574,-0.004794172,0.010009061],"hash":"2b5c9ded:1799","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-16T22:56:59.679Z\n- **User:** sera que nao tem a ver com isso? ele comeca com final .0.1 e so muda para 0.2 quando clico na sala\n- **Outcome:** Investigação fechada. Resposta direta: **não tem a ver com isso.** ## O `.0.1` → `.0.2` era só o rótulo mentindo `MainForm.cs:948` tinha o `127.0.0.1` **hardcoded** na string do `Status:` (e na linha 949 do log), enquanto o listener real usa `_instance.LocalIp` (`MainForm.cs:925-926` e `:936-937`). O `Status:` só \"vira\" `.0.2` quando o C116 chega e o listener do GS é criado (`MainForm.cs:939`) — daí a sua observação. Estado real dos sockets agora (verificado ao vivo): | Instância | CS | GS | CMD/PKT | |---|---|---|---| | base 100 (pid 8008) | **127.0.0.2**:44411 | **127.0.0.2**:45901 | 127.0.0.1:44512 / 44513 | | base 0 (pid 12940) | 127.0.0.1:44411 | 127.0.0.1:45901 | 127.0.0.1:44412 / 44413 | Isolamento perfeito, e o log do byp concorda: `connect local 127.0.0.2:44411 ret=0 err=0`. **Corrigido** (`MainForm.cs:948-949` agora usa `_instance.LocalIp`), Release compilado (0 erros) e `MuProxy2.dll` distribuído na raiz e nas duas sessões (164.352 bytes, 14:56:12). As 2 janinhas que estão abertas são do **bin\\Debug** e ainda mostram o rótulo antigo — para pegar a correção é preciso fechá-las e rebuildar (o `dotnet build -c Debug` falha com `MSB3021` porque o `MuProxy2.exe` está travado pelos processos 12940/8008). Me diz se quer que eu feche e rebuilde. ## O que REALMENTE trava a 2ª instância (e eu achei agora) O `Status:` não era o problema — **a conta da sessão base100 está obsoleta**: | Onde | base 0 | base 100 | |---|---|---| | `sessions\\*\\Settings.ini` (o que o cliente usa) |…\n- **Tools:** search_files, edit_file, read_file, run_command","vector":[0.059504066,0.047659967,-0.13758388,-0.013680435,0.08341506,-0.070405446,0.03461061,0.020065438,-0.03128618,-0.024468523,-0.056417402,0.0005979973,0.08052435,-0.021315997,0.04840715,-0.02691934,-0.015599739,-0.04053566,-0.05096346,0.038481858,0.023154015,-0.0066794236,-0.027647624,0.000097661534,0.101613276,0.07661785,0.0022742979,0.06691379,-0.047537163,-0.024431089,0.029864626,0.012418715,0.0347479,0.0047195945,-0.01687884,-0.061247505,-0.0017448704,-0.043604765,-0.012738258,-0.00952112,0.017963378,-0.07111119,0.010079053,-0.0032589517,0.0026780865,0.006471157,0.0147611825,0.03076236,0.08386182,-0.065404385,0.03224437,0.044838376,0.001452278,-0.020970587,0.08302517,0.029024603,-0.056013416,0.03400905,0.022261733,-0.037661836,0.08438862,-0.00054382085,-0.035785116,0.104095675,-0.019024316,-0.012850681,-0.035217308,0.0252282,-0.029292395,0.00016915394,0.038933787,0.009537843,0.03680367,0.009545366,-0.009534113,0.0039715096,-0.04128257,-0.030530564,0.0168653,0.012249368,0.0070365714,-0.0011686091,0.10349939,-0.0669392,0.030050144,-0.027351111,-0.03638557,-0.00448598,-0.029269993,0.08034031,0.009900974,-0.04072836,0.025371408,-0.03808504,-0.047266908,0.024156215,-0.05770937,0.015306653,-0.0020549197,-0.026608072,-0.044778533,-0.03827706,0.02078754,-0.012585748,0.027206242,0.09020252,0.012254996,0.0140753435,-0.019824367,-0.009063727,0.011587117,0.042237516,-0.021539906,-0.038220286,0.02066398,-0.022082755,0.04568914,-0.012690895,0.007040678,0.067527875,-0.051226866,-0.046852227,0.01910678,0.06558459,0.05425379,-0.015046295,-0.023809068,0.027895428,0.0654381,-0.05484059,-0.03816593,-0.00