me:** Duas provas, uma de cada vez. ## 1. O que o NOP fez de fato (memória do processo vivo, pid 364) ``` 0x6814E6B0 31 C0 90 90 90 90 ← patch do FindWindowA (xor eax,eax + 4 NOP) 0x6814E6B6 85 C0 test eax,eax 0x6814E6B8 0F 84 53 04 00 00 jz (inalterado) ... 0x6814E6E7 FF 15 E8 80 21 68 call [OpenMutexA] ← INTACTA 0x6814E6ED 85 C0 test eax,eax ← INTACTA 0x6814E6EF 90 90 90 90 90 90 ← NOSSO NOP (6 bytes) no lugar do jnz 0x6814E6F5 8D 44 24 18 lea eax,[esp+18h] ← caminho do CreateMutex INTACTO 0x6814E6FD FF 15 E4 80 21 68 call [CreateMutexA] ← INTACTA 0x6814E703 83 BE 1C 02 00 00 cmp dword [esi+21Ch],0 ← o fluxo segue normal ``` Foram **6 bytes, em um único salto**. A chamada do `OpenMutexA`, o `test`, o `CreateMutexA` e todo o resto do fluxo estão intactos — o NOP só remove o \"pulo para o `ExitProcess`\". Nenhum caminho de socket, de crypto ou de login é tocado por ele. (E o slot da IAT bateu certo até no build novo: `0x682180E8` = base + `0x2080E8`, o mesmo RVA do arquivo — a resolução por import table funcionou.) ## 2. O erro é ANTERIOR ao NOP Timeline do `byp.dll`: | hora | build em disco | o que aconteceu | |---|---|---| | 14:06:45 | **sem** o patch de mutex | — | | **14:25:16** | sem o patch de mutex | login → **`F1 01 02`** (AccountInvalid) | | **14:25:21 / :30** | sem o patch de mutex | → **`07`** → **`08`** (3 falhas, fecha) | | 14:51:55 | **com** o patch de mutex (meu) | — | | 14:52 / 14:54 | com o patch | greeting chegou, login → **`07`** | O \"Connection error\" / recusa de …\n- **Tools:** run_command, search_files","vector":[0.05344525,0.058029205,-0.1500027,-0.024564197,0.040773932,-0.07649884,0.03729528,0.006780087,-0.020001067,0.0013590244,-0.06658438,0.024647832,0.027066061,-0.0019524057,0.040916987,-0.018131575,-0.0038700039,-0.04701273,-0.060543824,0.026197148,0.05554115,-0.036185693,-0.031393535,0.017519731,0.09378498,0.0043579545,0.019079572,0.011968612,-0.042057317,-0.0068160077,0.06092401,0.0053562485,0.02148624,-0.021667238,-0.0024243111,-0.07