0674,0.026129276,-0.027264385,-0.056577098,-0.023076747,-0.0246975,0.05272045,-0.002765157,0.015901214,0.004393889,-0.018349497,-0.02160028,0.008331986,0.02127626,-0.014324965,0.022811938,-0.05128912,-0.045993764,0.02581215,0.00005703796,-0.00860614,0.026559198,0.015355091,0.11238752,0.029391373,-0.0049291635,-0.07962587,0.04885664,0.00858031,-0.03943993,-0.042317513,0.005090054,-0.011440475],"hash":"34f953af:1693","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-17T01:05:49.188Z\n- **User:** estou com xdbg aberto, procure oq gera o connection error.\n- **Outcome:** Respondo direto: **não era o x32dbg que eu estava depurando — era o `main.exe` do cliente.** O x32dbg é só a ferramenta (via MCP `xdbg32`). ## O que eu estava procurando O código do cliente que **exibe** o texto \"Connection error\" — para fechar a dúvida: o diálogo do seu screenshot vem - **(a)** do resultado de login `F1 01 07` (LoginResult 7 = \"ConnectionError\", recusa do Auth), ou - **(b)** da **queda do socket** (o \"dc\" que acabou de acontecer). São dois caminhos diferentes no cliente, e a resposta muda o diagnóstico. ## Como eu fui atrás 1. **A string não está em `main.exe` nem no `Main.dll`** (nem em ASCII, nem em UTF-16) → ela vem de **dados** (a tabela de mensagens do cliente, carregada sob demanda). Confirmou a intuição de \"talvez ela seja dinâmica\" — o cliente escolhe o texto **por índice**, não por endereço fixo. 2. No xdbg32, anexei no `main.exe` e armei: - `0x40B3D0` = **entrada da função de login** (o clique no OK) — BP que você mesmo colocou, e que disparou; - `0x40B454` = o `call` que **envia o login** (confirmado pelo stack do byp: `main.exe+0xB454` é o frame do envio, dentro dessa mesma função que começa em `+0xB3D0`); - `user32:MessageBoxA` = sonda — **não disparou**, confirmando que o diálogo é do próprio jogo (não é MessageBox do Windows); - **watchpoint de LEITURA** no byte do texto \"Connection error\" → dispara no instante em que o cliente busca o texto pra pintar → a pilha diria exatamente qual função gerou. 3. O watchpoint **disparou**, mas no **carrega…\n- **Tools:** skill, tool_search, search_files, run_command, mcp_tool, repl, desktop_list_windows, ask_user, desktop_snapshot, desktop_screenshot","vector":[0.056071084,0.09002247,-0.12039345,-0.052569356,0.03232199,-0.057122737,-0.000070408336,-0.013027325,-0.03349156,-0.039545827,-0.029699957,0.03574714,0.04330031,-0.034864906,0.025232488,-0.014894775,-0.0487427,-0.04424162,-0.052310776,-0.027163908,-0.010070614,-0.03212614,0.011167497,-0.013187337,0.09065543,0.026565412,0.0116308015,0.073930606,-0.08280833,0.010512824,0.0029745991,0.041870344,0.03085355,-0.019086357,-0.013217355,-0.051313538,-0.0068134684,-0.0012311568,-0.030173384,0.0191651,0.024682024,-0.09403549,0.0027068565,-0.0043153907,0.01440653,0.0036915678,0.027770476,0.07307377,0.06733167,-0.06712066,0.04650974,0.017292267,0.091308855,-0.05819586,0.10351659,0.049323406,-0.016813973,0.040455926,-0.008283442,-0.026583182,0.08522028,0.030664796,0.011905268,0.07509418,0.008555645,-0.0356567,-0.038359743,0.036325786,0.011414759,0.0032866145,0.044895124,-0.014433301,0.018483438,0.0084895715,0.008714838,-0.004752395,-0.028553436,-0.047283363,0.033250973,0.010570218,0.006114971,0.008135056,0.06497431,-0.048976615,0.036548056,-0.01775245,-0.048193056,0.0052399263,-0.024282103,0.06561317,0.02590488,-0.028841125,0.022233976,-0.0020291475,-0.07194793,0.007344632,-0.039469693,0.046050932,0.0043210806,-0.036958713,-0.031136012,-0.0015027545,0.023802016,0.02616234,-0.000842679,0.07753526,0.016497893,0.0028239337,-0.008417257,-0.0076109995,-0.019005748,0.037571166,-0.005359543,-0.067363374,0.0019353109,-0.0000806189,0.041297246,-0.014437215,0.014570335,0.022077924,-0.04094485,-0.02594109,0.0064971675,0.051346306,0.04485307,0.017447883,-0.03203275,0.027124736,0.03099126,-0.064136,-0.024345275,-0.031063128,-0.03339519,0.015938122,0.024520067,-0.0175156