 CHEGOU (slot novo 0x332D/0x32DB/0x33DB) GS: CGConnectAccountRecv → manda conta/senha/IP pro Auth ↓ Auth responde o resultado → JSProtocol repassa pro cliente (JSProtocol.cpp:72-76) ↓ cliente recebeu C1 05 F1 01 <result> → 02 → 07 → 08 ↓ cliente pega o texto do índice na tabela de mensagens (\"Connection error\" = LoginResult 7) ↓ dialogo \"Connection error\" ``` ## O que está PROVADO (com o dado) | # | Fato | Evidência | |---|---|---| | 1 | **O GS aceitou a 2ª conexão TCP** | `recv() ret=12` → `[C1 0C F1 00 01 33 2D 33 31 2E 00 00]` (log base100:1341-1342). Esse pacote é o `GCConnectClientSend` (`Protocol.cpp:2941-2950`), enviado em `SocketManager.cpp:811`, **depois** do `gObjAdd` (`:763`) e do `CheckIpAddress` (`:719`) | | 2 | A recusa foi **depois**, no login | `[C1 05 F1 01 02]` → `[07]` → `[08]` (base100:1515, 1564, 1628) — `GCConnectAccountSend` (`Protocol.cpp:2968-2988`) | | 3 | O **8 = \"3 falhas\"** do servidor | `JSProtocol.cpp:74`: `LoginMessageCount>=3 ? 8 : result` — bate exatamente com as 3 tentativas | | 4 | A **base 0 entrou** (`F1 01 01`) com o mesmo código, mesmo build, mesmos patches | base0:271, 1…\n- **Tools:** search_files, read_file","vector":[0.031829774,0.06475939,-0.14631087,-0.06370659,0.065986045,-0.051606048,0.034722794,-0.029827747,-0.04524,-0.03530134,-0.059965715,-0.0027684937,0.04535746,-0.024564682,0.038480222,-0.005565119,-0.052140363,-0.03524154,-0.096744806,0.009057209,-0.0127834175,-0.04029511,-0.0173898,-0.017072247,0.08056006,0.029738048,-0.01754792,0.048731275,-0.06155896,-0.019825011,0.03217148,0.03670764,0.027926272,-0.025648285,-0.035661142,-0.030820167,0.034755222,-0.026535893,-0.0033604417,0.009852128,0.0356759,-0.08426079,-0.025724541,0.011328835,-0.0047602905,0.016379211,0.03566109,0.06112464,0.03980201,-0.08491742,0.042828582,0.043178335,-0.0011506473,-0.015324379,0.081308946,0.04083522,-0.01634674,0.017222958,0.02356773,-0.04780999,0.10240344,0.009617424,0.021432271,0.076650836,0.00529692,-0.030273909,-0.054410856,0.