,-0.0077033592,0.0626739,0.0016737074,-0.050484855,0.013081923,0.011480593,-0.007219552,-0.011205408,-0.046429213,-0.022027588,-0.003108119,-0.0032726708,-0.022752158,-0.04783481,0.028672757,0.012332543,-0.009249006,-0.027790794,-0.011945481,0.04197233,-0.010363974,0.017608894,-0.011799871,-0.0011738848,-0.042873304,-0.04551661,-0.071034364,0.06674275,-0.0023386283,0.02016529,0.028867235,-0.0057405066,-0.008465995,-0.026664669,0.01385799,0.014650535,0.047719806,-0.012985699,-0.021385701,0.017455062,-0.015673917,0.0011987926,0.008387666,0.043529972,0.09861275,0.01947127,-0.004402096,-0.057384532,0.054796677,0.02266083,0.025513025,-0.036731496,-0.0370949,0.016572295],"hash":"24a48244:1829","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-17T01:16:03.468Z\n- **User:** mas ambas contas existem evtnlife e evtnlife1\n- **Outcome:** Dado novo e importante. Ele muda a lista de candidatos — e deixa o cerco fechar em **3 regras de servidor**, todas verificáveis. ## O que continua PROVADO (não muda com essa informação) 1. **O GS aceitou a 2ª conexão** — greeting de 12 bytes com slot novo (`0x332D`/`0x32DB`/`0x33CE`), que é o `GCConnectClientSend` enviado **depois** do `gObjAdd` (`SocketManager.cpp:763`→`:811`). ⇒ Não foi `CF_REJECT`/limite por IP. 2. **A recusa foi do Auth, no login**: `C1 05 F1 01 02` → `07` → `08`. O `08` é literalmente o \"3 falhas → fecha\" do `JSProtocol.cpp:74`. O GS **repassa o resultado do Auth sem alterar** (`JSProtocol.cpp:72-76`) → quem decidiu foi o Auth. 3. **As contas são diferentes**: o bloco de conta do login diverge (cipher determinístico — o da base0 é byte-idêntico nas 6 entradas dela), e o `.\\Settings.ini` que o cliente lê (CWD = sessão) diz `evtnlife` na base100 e `evtnlife1` na base0. 4. **As duas instâncias batem no mesmo IP público** (`186.235.202.26`) — o socket de saída é do MuProxy2 (`TcpLoopbackProxy.cs:219-220`), então o loopback não muda o IP visto pelo GS. 5. **Loopback, NOPs e mutex inocentados**: base0 roda o mesmo build com os mesmos patches e entra (`F1 01 01`). ## O que a informação nova elimina - ❌ \"A conta não existe\" → eliminada (você confirmou que `evtnlife` existe). - ❌ \"Senha errada\" → o código do servidor seria **0** (`InvalidPassword`), e veio **2**. - ❌ \"Bloqueada\" → seria **5** (e 10/11/14 para casos de expiry). - ❌ \"Servidor cheio\" → **4**. - ❌ \"V…\n- **Tools:** search_files, read_file, repl","vector":[0.028746214,0.062234566,-0.14265263,-0.027670652,0.068260595,-0.02667397,-0.0016812168,0.022918016,-0.060582932,0.0033534588,-0.06862578,0.0065548215,0.050822638,-0.003227042,0.0074067186,-0.0075226105,0.000013448172,-0.04281504,-0.03407302,0.037099153,-0.0035068486,-0.030668676,-0.050936606,0.03797775,0.08722211,0.040065452,0.015904073,0.085623235,-0.043062415,-0.026417049,0.04026091,0.05808139,0.025109144,-0.046895396,-0.030117184,-0.022888565,-0.008691113,-0.013022707,-0.031230634,-0.004106279,0.038340155,-0.0539283,-0.03457961,-0.02124844,0.018413125,0.028801939,0.045766078,0.016648272,0.06620472,-0.11265185,0.037057694,0.05951566,0.031175658,-0.041170437,0.101472385,0.0056143277,-0.045915246,0.055115946,-0.0030695943,-0.019837566,0.07494121,-0.008176705,-0.005383342,0.0714118,0.0412728,-0.020269148,-0.051906917,0.047711276,-0.03080818,-0.0011933754,0.042107373,0.009262086,0.008714188,0.028778058,0.005459023,-0.004272875,-0.028841738,-0.051612325,0.0009524926,0.017396947,0.011941738,0.00964369,0.059793927,-0.057808075,0.04574176,-0.008723838,-0.017789992,0.0053424425,-0.03431993,0.0846182,-0.0068863765,-0.017838033,0.024673218,-0.0006779885,-0.039212257,0.0514302,-0.04899789,-0.0073527484,-0.034955055,-0.010349143,-0.02023827,-0.05781356,0.033450212,-0.030253598,0.028047418,0.019387603,0.03427138,-0.010915079,0.012877361,-0.021303264,-0.012033261,0.03715108,-0.06091745,-0.049130492,0.026893819,0.0009036324,0.028488455,-0.03203855,-0.013061969,0.052542467,-0.026567698,-0.0088742