.022281006,-0.0006113299,-0.0046019736,0.02114799,0.008174679,-0.030437976,-0.0026977814,0.03562188,-0.003764202,-0.03435529,-0.0071161822,0.035136588,0.0026390345,-0.005553338,-0.054987725,-0.08909534,-0.058066696,-0.010223798,0.016063506,-0.022855429,0.019611565,0.002159049,0.0012115368,0.124946564,0.027046915,-0.044092394,-0.015927661,0.0043324516,-0.0047794343,0.0040816474,0.04594555,-0.007084426,-0.05732771,0.027059333,-0.02689938,-0.020596849,0.003818771,-0.047723252,0.011263297,0.031656157,-0.042871267,-0.044267207,0.02073253,0.0010244437,-0.044525746,0.012337093,0.0057062055,-0.009494929,0.0057734437,-0.030829255,0.027158346,-0.04229359,0.0005421764,-0.04555017,0.00937246,-0.05469509,-0.0092758965,0.0072574667,0.020609867,-0.046963666,0.04230397,0.0052555585,0.012032822,0.02063688,-0.030633949,0.00537814,0.00079390744,-0.00026545732,0.0013756754,-0.026327793,-0.00068224623,-0.01651894,0.0036367683,0.022919316,-0.031252403,0.0046741595,0.01777965,0.02755601,-0.027514584,-0.01352777,0.0432665,0.0035894457,-0.0034809269,-0.015520766,-0.023872955,-0.039762694,-0.024194127,-0.013315612,0.009693617,-0.0035257488,0.031194149,0.025738532,-0.0067329514,0.0033225396,-0.01691264,-0.04109178,0.0019670832,0.049632806,-0.014246974,-0.03369349,0.023056757,-0.005107837,-0.024783026,-0.018227074,0.019591887,0.112797655,0.024651686,-0.0029808034,-0.051815078,0.014064859,-0.002310235,0.022516388,-0.072170384,-0.04253695,0.031688336],"hash":"3c09adb5:1743","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-17T01:37:00.855Z\n- **User:** se eles tem bloqueio nao [e so ip, tem hwid ou outra coisa no meio para identificar e isso que preciso de ajuda para desobrir... pois veja bem tenho dois computadores usando o mesmo roteador, saindo para mesmo ip publico e funciona dois clientes. no mesmo computador ao clicar na sala e preencher user e senha da esse connection error. antes de mudarmos o loopback para 127.0.0.2 ele ja fechava ao selecionar sala. agora o erro e outro. me ajuda investigar.\n- **Outcome:** Analisei tudo que dá para extrair do lado do cliente. Aqui está o que está **comprovado** e o que falta confirmar no servidor. ## O que o cliente envia que identifica a máquina **1. O cliente gera um HWID — confirmado nos logs.** ``` [2026-11-16 12:56:12] [HWID] cliente gerou o HWID: 12BA1074-DE8E4EB3-BC5BDE2E-BFCE2022 [2026-11-16 13:06:34] [HWID] cliente gerou o HWID: 12BA1074-DE8E4EB3-BC5BDE2E-BFCE2022 ``` Mesmo valor nas duas execuções → é derivado da máquina (volume serial / UUID / CPU, como no `GetHardwareId.cpp` do eMU). É o **mesmo** nas duas instâncias no mesmo PC, e **diferente** entre os dois PCs. **2. O HWID NÃO vai em claro no tráfego.** Procurei `12BA1074...` (ASCII e hex) em todo o `gg_bypass2.log` da base100 → zero ocorrências. Ele vai **dentro do payload cifrado** do pacote de login. **3. O pacote de login tem ~34 bytes a mais que o struct padrão do eMU.** - eMU `PMSG_CONNECT_ACCOUNT_SEND`: account[10] + password[12] + tick[4] + version[5] + serial[16] = **47 bytes** - Payload real (após `C1 5F F1`): **81 bytes** - Diferença: **34 bytes** ≈ o tamanho de um HWID de 36 chars (se o password for 10 em vez de 12, fecha exato: 10+10+4+5+16+36 = 81) **4. Comparação byte a byte dos dois logins (base0 × base100):** ``` bytes 0–8 : IDÊNTICOS (0E 8F 15 0F 3E 57 A6 FD 9B) bytes 9–80 : TODOS DIFERENTES ``` Os bytes 9+ diferem **inclusive na senha** (que é a mesma `395739` nos dois) → o trecho a partir do byte 9 é cifrado com algo por-sessão. Os bytes 0–8 são constantes (he…\n- **Tools:** search_files, read_file, list_directory, run_command, repl","vector":[0.03890223,0.06456029,-0.14697604,-0.032270603,0.035914194,-0.06004637,0.03742836,0.0055427616,-0.05096053,-0.03127048,-0.044286653,0.011629498,0.017849535,-0.026768247,0.050233074,-0.0075174924,-0.015903426,-0.0572054,-0.03869807,0.033763364,-0.035540108,-0.010710177,-0.07905694,0.0010520075,0.058320697