22,0.038593322,-0.030523414,0.015440098,0.02596064,0.03214837,0.08573968,0.018905887,-0.051731143,-0.008373809,-0.036138713,0.013609765,-0.029303014,0.019773081,-0.015809119,-0.041553043,-0.0021218783,-0.041938256,0.015097915,-0.026497474,-0.03724272,-0.029987877,-0.0034789,-0.04724921,-0.045253906,0.035866857,0.0072125723,-0.042818822,-0.00941359,0.04320258,-0.03521271,0.032766618,0.0074443994,0.064362,-0.011682908,0.008333518,-0.04673448,-0.0074050077,-0.0404805,-0.02304268,-0.026836414,-0.017747682,-0.07378972,0.006577282,0.015790705,0.020545505,0.019249389,-0.04742772,0.00073846517,-0.017733097,0.034082234,0.017816102,-0.0670119,-0.021677136,-0.009042547,0.0015593298,-0.0061518652,-0.018139927,-0.0028431725,-0.016721949,0.0025168092,-0.016807439,-0.008112705,0.03543053,-0.010401929,0.011532971,-0.023339141,-0.024747618,-0.047865264,-0.032517638,-0.0216965,0.00287967,-0.016607858,0.01212189,0.034678373,-0.029443191,0.008072529,-0.022587039,-0.015288704,-0.019662224,0.0599821,-0.010802302,-0.05310239,0.051275548,-0.009412726,0.012774742,0.00937709,0.038350947,0.122684196,0.0442354,-0.00900761,-0.060677536,0.028233305,0.03582176,0.0031892934,-0.046068966,-0.023631265,0.034807887],"hash":"d8ece7ee:2086","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-17T01:40:59.752Z\n- **User:** me ajude fixar meu o byp, preciso que em cada instancia do main.exe ele abra com um hwid unico.\n- **Outcome:** Não vou implementar isso. Gerar um HWID falso por instância no cliente é exatamente o tipo de override/spoofing de HWID que você mesmo registrou que não quer — e, na prática, é contornar a trava anti‑multibox do servidor pelo lado errado. Deixa eu ser direto sobre o porquê e sobre o que resolve de verdade: **Por que não pelo cliente** - O servidor recusa a 2ª sessão (`F1 01 07`). Forjar o HWID no cliente só faria o servidor \"ver\" outra máquina — é burlar a regra dele, não corrigir nada. - É frágil: se o servidor também olha outro sinal (conta já conectada, IP, serial do cliente, HWID em outra tabela), o spoof quebra no próximo passo e você fica sem saber por quê. - Você administra o servidor. O caminho limpo é mudar a regra lá, não mentir para ela. **O que resolve (e eu te ajudo)** Como você tem acesso ao servidor, o ajuste certo é no lado dele: 1. Confirmar **qual** regra dispara — o log do JoinServer/AuthServer (ou a tabela de contas/`AuthLog`) mostra o motivo exato da recusa às 15:13:03 para `evtnlife`. É lá que aparece \"HWID já em uso\", \"conta já conectada\", \"HWID não autorizado\", etc. 2. Com o motivo em mãos, relaxar/whitelistar a regra para a sua máquina (ex.: permitir N sessões por HWID, ou liberar o seu HWID `12BA1074-DE8E4EB3-BC5BDE2E-BFCE2022`). Isso te dá as duas instâncias sem forjar nada, e sem depender de o cliente \"mentir\" melhor que o servidor. **O que eu posso fazer agora** - Te guiar na leitura do log do servidor para achar a linha exata da recusa (me diga o…\n- **Tools:** none","vector":[0.043689728,0.06183182,-0.17569716,0.0015679053,0.045881994,-0.056012582,0.05664822,0.036523744,-0.014600665,-0.033106714,-0.03214472,-0.00012181424,0.026221981,-0.02508228,0.022920704,0.013788803,-0.00042182775,-0.05572776,-0.0509055,0.010131308,-0.032510992,-0.0505336,-0.06929222,0.023641018,0.061745536,0.038669284,0.020573745,0.052108664,-0.006480839,-0.00682217,0.0363512,0.059575208,0.039989147,-0.033915896,0.028545048,-0.008398242,0.032043375,-0.006060021,-0.02190794,0.037383106,0.0074307593,-0.04291194,0.034131117,-0.01267982,0.032363854,0.024101842,0.036504224,0.037687477,0.07418387,-0.04481021,0.06780991,-0.0014013979,0.012015043,-0.07038035,0.096910484,-0.022246767,-0.058772355,0.03579195,-0.01767105,-0.012787956,0.0443796,0.040100385,0.010013058,0.078504786,-0.04977562,-0.019704415,-0.054829583,0.020559175,-0.0036525247,-0.021591883,0.06569321,-0.0009142704,0.05610818,-0.0006149199,-0.012837658,-0.022289963,-0.022623079,-0.04094602,0