016692372,0.036515396,0.038353924,-0.019587286,0.0106818825,-0.031098334,0.02469373,-0.048559435,0.004480301,0.034082197,-0.016954927,0.004528934,-0.011205014,-0.034485564,-0.053651225,-0.032889266,-0.011440781,0.002259415,-0.00821801,0.008235013,-0.006299365,-0.024134213,0.029754102,-0.017845452,-0.03810936,-0.018344209,0.030831648,-0.024193699,-0.046646733,0.015729265,0.012597217,0.028154822,0.0038911316,0.027287807,0.11566105,0.060801335,-0.015577288,-0.07994701,-0.004803073,0.021165874,-0.006769356,-0.051537953,-0.00028358446,0.012670155],"hash":"5418db8a:1670","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-17T01:42:32.368Z\n- **User:** o blackrock ta na minha outra maquina o server e meu.\n- **Outcome:** Entendi — o servidor é seu e está na outra máquina. Isso muda o caminho certo, mas não muda o fato de que forjar HWID no cliente continua sendo a ferramenta errada — e vai contra o que você mesmo registrou (\"HWID só se diagnostica server-side, sem override no cliente\"). Sendo direto: **Se o servidor é seu, você não precisa mentir para ele.** A regra que barra a 2ª sessão (seja \"uma sessão por HWID\", \"conta já conectada\", ou o que for) está no seu servidor. O conserto limpo é afrouxar/whitelistar essa regra lá — não fazer o cliente fingir ser outra máquina. Forjar HWID no byp: - não corrige nada, só mascara; - é frágil (se o servidor também olha conta/IP/serial, quebra no passo seguinte); - e transforma o byp numa ferramenta de evasão de HWID, que é exatamente o que você disse não querer. **O que eu preciso saber para te ajudar de verdade** — como é esse servidor seu? 1. **É código que você pode alterar/recompilar** (ex.: o eMU/BlackrockMU a partir do fonte)? → eu te aponto exatamente onde fica a checagem (no eMU de referência é o `GJConnectAccountRecv` em `JoinServerProtocol.cpp`, que devolve \"já conectado\"; o `07` é código próprio do BlackrockMU, então o ponto exato está no seu fonte/log) e como liberar N sessões por HWID ou whitelistar o seu. 2. **É binário fechado que você não recompila?** → aí o caminho é achar a config/DB que controla o limite (muitos servidores têm `.ini` ou tabela de contas com flag de HWID/limite de sessões), ou o log do JoinServer/AuthServer que most…\n- **Tools:** none","vector":[0.028460192,0.044921834,-0.17462766,-0.00082596054,0.045729034,-0.06419393,0.05486286,0.039926656,-0.05456147,-0.0020281577,-0.03717826,0.05285334,0.023609994,-0.0005017966,0.030991537,0.004816135,0.00045815695,-0.011719926,-0.04694593,0.015203121,-0.033380363,-0.02665849,-0.036773622,0.015759358,0.08562349,0.024894599,0.02720864,0.057258334,-0.04698617,-0.016728912,0.033163786,0.05893816,0.038149077,-0.006886479,0.02331905,-0.00768948,0.0066055106,-0.0014295598,-0.02161968,0.016406534,0.036291223,-0.078424424,-0.0109315775,-0.061234985,0.043414082,0.0076591894,0.02917532,0.023404839,0.06140318,-0.06571377,0.07431664,-0.0044905385,0.04090679,-0.040505547,0.07121255,-0.01292783,-0.01648582,0.054913066,-0.005460827,0.009363498,0.045033537,0.0023029456,-0.034803983,0.12428366,-0.02385484,0.007754716,-0.05474309,0.03579519,-0.03575336,-0.018755596,0.043619838,-0.0040498795,0.042857353,0.010312099,-0.005612956,-0.039940644,-0.05053339,-0.037311878,0.0007697602,-0.049388602,0.01876607,0.030075388,0.067968935,-0.014515501,0.050257634,0.030726876,-0.025148675,0.03723021,-0.06188026,0.04604735,0.015288471,-0.042761575,0.025619354,0.0023800554,-0.04817559,-0.011524841,-0.050530117,0.024941437,-0.012339919,-0.01286866,-0.020534065,-0.013527778,-0.0009276646,-0.008734069,0.046882503,0.022367323,0.0074752076,0.031859916,-0.029788591,-0.03344553,0.01359144,0.015046156,-0.020419365,-0.046406355,0.03882165,-0.03928138,0.02895736,-0.013582456,-0.024239851,0.063746676,-0.04094522,-0.027622374,-0.028693542,0.07246767,0.056999076,0.0130800875,-0.059385978,0.06510608,0.021852326,-0.04818431,-0.01027422,-0.0371947,-0.070670076,0.06283276,0.014923