rite.cpp` + `src/include/HwidRewrite.h`), ligado no `HookSend` (`WinsockHooks.cpp`) e inicializado no `dllmain.cpp`. A cada `send()`, ele: 1. Decifra Layer-1 do pacote; 2. Se for um **C3** (login), decifra o SimpleModulus → pacote interno `C1 5F F1 …`; 3. Desfaz o Camada-2 (`UnXorData`) no payload; 4. Procura o HWID (`XXXXXXXX-XXXXXXXX-XXXXXXXX-XXXXXXXX`, 35 chars) — confirmado no seu log em offset ~59 do pacote interno; 5. Troca pelo HWID **desta instância** e re-cifra tudo (XorData → SM → Layer-1); 6. **Verificação fail-safe**: decifra o pacote reescrito e confere o HWID novo; se qualquer etapa falhar, envia o pacote **original** sem alteração. **Derivação por instância** (determinística, sem estado): - base `0` → HWID real (nada muda); - base `>0` → HWID real com o último DWORD XOR `base * 2654435761` (ex.: base 100 → `…-7265A906`); - override manual: variável de ambiente `MUPROXY_HWID=XXXXXXXX-…` força um HWID específico. **Build**: `byp.dll` recompilada e copiada para `F:\\blackrockmu\\byp.dll`. O `main.exe` foi fechado pelo build — precisa reabrir o jogo. ## Verificação feita - Round-trip do SimpleModulus com as chaves reais do seu log: **OK** (vetor `01..08 → 0D 5F…` confere). - Pipeline completo simulado em Python (Layer-1 → SM → XorData → troca → re-cifra): **OK** para base 0/100/200, com o resto do payload intacto…\n- **Tools:** skill, list_directory, search_files, read_file, ask_user, manage_todos, write_file, edit_file, run_command, tool_search, memory","vector":[0.04573628,0.05132438,-0.14260714,-0.0203338,0.06575983,-0.081407286,0.03729734,0.04041498,-0.06866221,-0.060340427,-0.042928915,0.012215246,0.055115692,-0.029698262,0.030089814,0.020499934,-0.006775199,-0.052111767,-0.04474218,0.041569877,-0.026243396,-0.050344314,-0.07976097,0.009867537,0.07559106,0.04114391,-0.015234903,0.040241953,-0.042843007,-0.027828528,0.047082487,0.019900449,0.025954308,-0.055667367,-0.030864421,-0.01364273,0.03181443,-0.0506484,-0.01341009,0.026536414,0.03083744,-0.048